 {:seon.task/name "a-persons-code-owes-no-wiki-citation"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-10 measuring the request agent (a root from jolt/request-launch, three home requests to add demo.math/triple with a test): of the three launched agents two merged and one, request/add-a-function-demo-536871029 (agent a5c60f647c9c6fc2), never wrote its test: after defining triple it spent its turns finding a wiki section to cite, `(doc \"docs/prompt.md#the-program-is-your-branchs-facts\")`, a d/q for :wiki/path holding demo, `(search \"wiki citation docstring entry\")`, app.calc's docstrings; run 0's agent did the same through `(cite/check 'demo.math/triple)`. The cause, read on its branch: the write-back gave the person's new namespace a file, src/demo/math.clj, so seon.program/program-nss counts it as the program's own and seon.problems/uncited-vars holds an open row 'demo.math/triple is public and its docstring cites no docs/ section: cite the one that describes it'. The citation law is about Seon's own program (AGENTS.md section 7); Seon does any work its user wants, and a person's code has no mechanism in the wiki to cite. The change: uncited-vars judges a namespace the wiki describes, known by data the namespace already holds: its ns docstring cites a docs/ section (every Seon namespace's does, AGENTS.md section 7), so a namespace made for a person's work, with no such citation, is not judged; the prompt says the same in one line (the citation rule binds the program's code you change; new code of the person's has a docstring that says what it is, no citation owed). Proofs: uncited-vars on a branch holding demo.math (a file under src/, no ns docstring citing a section) answers no row, and on a Seon namespace whose var cites nothing it answers its row, as today; and one curated request of plain user work merges with no eval searching for a section to cite (the held agent's evals are the reproduction)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
